<title>UK: Aluminium stocks fall in April - IPAI.</title>
<headline>Aluminium stocks fall in April - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total stocks of all forms of aluminium at Western world smelters excluding finished end-products, fell to 3.047 million tonnes at the end of April 1997, compared with 3.096 million in March and 3.514 million in April 1996, provisional International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) figures show.</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks fell to 1.536 million tonnes versus 1.562 million and 1.923 million, respectively.  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of the total aluminium stocks was as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			    Apr'97   Mar'97    Apr'96</p>
<p>    Africa		    62	 64	  85</p>
<p>    North America	1,436    1,473     1,695</p>
<p>    Latin America	  149	152	 178</p>
<p>    Asia		     148	135	 177</p>
<p>    Europe		 1,119    1,133     1,218</p>
<p>    Oceania		  133	139	 161</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks were distributed as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			    Apr'97    Mar'97    Apr'96</p>
<p>    Africa		    24	 20	  35</p>
<p>    North America	  610	632	 806</p>
<p>    Latin America	   99	102	 131</p>
<p>    Asia		     109	 98	 153</p>
<p>    Europe		   604	614	 672</p>
<p>    Oceania		   90	 96	 126</p>
<p>--London Newsroom 44 171 542 8080</p>
</text>
